Here’s what the response would look like if you queried VirusTotal for subdomains of **example.org** with a limit of 10 and a continuation cursor of `abc`.  
(Replace the placeholder IDs and attributes with the actual values returned by the API.)

```json
[
  {
    "id": "sub1.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "type": "subdomain",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "first_seen": "2024-01-15T12:34:56Z"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "sub2.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "type": "subdomain",
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "first_seen": "2024-02-03T08:21:00Z"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "sub3.example.org"
  },
  {
    "id": "sub4.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "type": "subdomain",
      "confidence": 0.92
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "sub5.example.org"
  },
  {
    "id": "sub6.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "type": "subdomain",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "last_seen": "2024-03-10T14:00:00Z"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "sub7.example.org"
  },
  {
    "id": "sub8.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "type": "subdomain",
      "confidence": 0.90
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "sub9.example.org"
  },
  {
    "id": "sub10.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "type": "subdomain",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "first_seen": "2024-04-01T09:15:30Z"
    }
  }
]
```

**How to retrieve this data**

```bash
curl -X GET \
  "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related_objects?relationship=subdomains&limit=10&continuation_cursor=abc" \
  -H "x-apikey: my_api"
```

The API will return a JSON payload similar to the one above. Extract each object’s `id` and, if present, its `attributes.context_attributes`. If an object has no `context_attributes`, simply omit that field or set it to `null`.
